      "Link to Wondr Health website\nShare:\nFull Stack Engineer\nRemote - Dallas, TX\n$130,000 ‒ $150,000 Hourly\nEngineering\nDEPARTMENT:\n\nProduct Engineering\n\nPOSITION:\n\nFull Stack Engineer\n\nREPORTS TO:\n\nTech Lead, Senior Software Engineer\n\nSUPERVISES:\n\nNone\n\nJOB CLASS:\n\nExempt\n\nPURPOSE:\nWe're looking for a Full-Stack Engineer to join our product engineering team. You'll work across the stack — from frontend interfaces to backend services — building features and systems that directly improve the health journey of our participants. \n\nThis isn't a heads-down, ticket-taking role. We're looking for someone who thinks beyond the immediate task: someone who asks \"why\" before jumping to \"how,\" and who's excited to grow into owning technical design decisions. You'll work closely with our engineering manager and collaborate with the team to shape how we build — not just what we build.\n\n\n\nESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS:\nBuild and maintain features across our full stack (PHP, Vue, React Native, AWS Serverless)\nCollaborate on Technical Requirements Documents (TDRs) and contribute to system design discussions\nParticipate in architecture decisions and help evaluate trade-offs as our systems evolve\nWrite clean, testable code and participate in thorough code reviews\nPartner with product and design to translate user needs into thoughtful technical solutions\nLeverage agentic AI workflows to accelerate development, automate repetitive tasks, and enhance your productivity\nHelp improve our development processes, tooling, and documentation over time\nWhat Success Looks Like:\n\nIn your first 30 days: You're onboarded, shipping small PRs, reviewing your team’s PRs, and building context on our systems and codebase.\nBy 90 days: You're independently owning features end-to-end and actively contributing to TRDs and design conversations.\nBy 6 months: You're a go-to contributor on the team — proposing technical approaches, identifying system-level improvements, and helping raise the bar for the team.\nWhy Wondr:\n\nMission that matters. The code you write directly affects people's health outcomes.\nFully remote. Work from wherever you do your best thinking.\nGrowth opportunity. You'll have a clear path from strong mid-level contributor to senior engineer with system design ownership. \nCollaborative culture. Small team, low ego, high trust.\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS:\nEducation:\n\nBachelor’s degree in a technology field preferred but not required.\n\nExperience:\n\nRequired:\n\n3–5 years of professional software development experience across frontend and backend\n\nSolid working experience with at least two of: PHP, Vue, React Native, AWS Serverless (Lambda, API Gateway, DynamoDB, etc.)\n\nComfort working across the full stack — you don't need to be an expert in everything, but you're willing to go wherever the problem takes you\n\nExperience contributing to or writing technical documentation (TDRs, design docs, ADRs, or similar)\n\nStrong communication skills — you can explain your thinking clearly to both technical and non-technical teammates\n\nA systems-thinking mindset: you consider how pieces fit together, not just the piece in front of you\n\nExperience with or enthusiasm for agentic AI workflows (e.g., AI-assisted coding, automated testing, prompt-driven development) — this is part of how we work at Wondr\n\nPreferred:\n\nExperience with health tech, wellness platforms, or mission-driven products\n\nFamiliarity with mobile development workflows (React Native in particular)\n\nExperience mentoring junior developers or leading small technical initiatives\n\nExposure to CI/CD pipelines, cloud infrastructure, or DevOps practices\n\n\n\nJOB CODE: 1000010\nGet Updates\nAre you interested in hearing about new opportunities at Wondr Health in real time? Enter your email address to be notified automatically when new positions are posted.\nEnter your email address\nPowered by ExponentATS © 2026 | Privacy Policy\nAdmin Login | Subscribe via RSS\n",
