      "Software Engineer II\n﻿\nLinkedInTwitterEmailMessageShare\nInformation Technology --> Engineering/Architecture\n\nRemote  •  ID:\n1173-383\n  •  Full-Time/Regular\n\n \nCore4ce LLC, a Data-Minded National Security Partner, is seeking a Software Engineer II to join the Autonomy, Artificial Intelligence, and Machine Learning (AAIM) Lab and contribute to a data analysis platform supporting Department of Defense (DoD) and Intelligence Community (IC) mission customers. This is a hands-on engineering role embedded within a small, fast-moving team where you will design, build, and ship production software — not sit behind layers of abstraction. The ideal candidate is a versatile software engineer who is comfortable working across the stack, from cloud infrastructure and containerized services to backend APIs and data pipelines. You should be the kind of engineer who builds things on the side, contributes to open source, and takes ownership of problems end-to-end. You will work closely with government customers and mission partners, so the ability to translate user needs into working software quickly and iteratively is essential.\n\n \n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\n\nPlatform Development & Engineering\n\nDesign, develop, and maintain software components for a data analysis platform supporting DoD/IC customers\nBuild and optimize backend services, APIs, and data pipelines using Python\n Implement containerized microservices architectures using Docker, deploying via AWS ECS and Lambda.\n Develop and manage database solutions (DynamoDB, RDS/PostgreSQL, or equivalent) for structured and semi-structured data at scale\n Write clean, well-tested, and well-documented code following modern software engineering best practices\n \n\nCloud Infrastructure & DevOps\n\nProvision and manage AWS cloud infrastructure using Infrastructure as Code (CloudFormation).\nBuild and maintain CI/CD pipelines for automated testing, deployment, and environment management\n Implement monitoring, logging, and alerting for production services\nSupport cloud environments across both commercial AWS and AWS GovCloud as required by program needs\nManage container registries, networking configurations, and security group policies\n \n\nCustomer Engagement & Delivery\n\nWork directly with government customers and end users to understand requirements, gather feedback, and iterate on solutions\nParticipate in agile development cycles including sprint planning, standups, demos, and retrospectives\nDeliver working software incrementally, prioritizing user value and mission impact over perfection\n Support technical demonstrations, program reviews, and customer engagements as needed\nCommunicate technical decisions and trade-offs clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholders\n \n\nCollaboration & Team Contribution\n\nOperate as a core contributor within a small, high-tempo engineering team where every team member’s output matters\nConduct and participate in code reviews, architecture discussions, and technical planning\nContribute to shared tooling, documentation, and internal engineering standards\nSupport integration with broader AAIM Lab capabilities including AI/ML pipelines, data fusion systems, and analytics tools\n \n\nREQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS:\n\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Computer Engineering, or a closely related STEM discipline\n2–5 years of professional software engineering experience building and shipping production applications\nStrong proficiency in one or more high-level languages: Python, JavaScript/TypeScript, Go, or equivalent\nHands-on AWS experience including\n- Containerized services (ECS, EKS, Fargate, or similar)\n\n-  Database services (DynamoDB, RDS, Aurora, or similar)\n\n- Infrastructure as Code (CloudFormation, Terraform, CDK, or similar)\n\nPractical experience building, managing, and deploying Docker containers in production environments\nProficiency with Git including branching strategies, pull requests, and collaborative workflows\nU.S. Citizenship required; must be able to obtain and maintain a DoD Secret security clearance\n*This position is designed to be flexible, with responsibilities evolving to meet business needs and enable individual growth.\n\n \n\nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:\n\nStrongly Preferred\n\nDemonstrated history of personal projects, side builds, or open-source contributions with a public commit history (GitHub, GitLab, etc.)\n Experience working in small, fast-paced teams (startup-like or skunkworks environments) where engineers own problems end-to-end\n Direct experience working with customers or end users — not abstracted behind multiple layers of product management\nActive DoD Secret clearance\n \n\nNice to Have\n\nExperience with data pipeline frameworks (Apache Airflow, Step Functions, Prefect, or similar)\nFamiliarity with data analysis or visualization tools and libraries (Pandas, Plotly, D3.js, etc.)\nExperience with serverless architectures (Lambda, API Gateway, EventBridge)\nFamiliarity with Kubernetes beyond managed offerings (cluster management, Helm charts, service mesh)\nExposure to AI/ML systems, model serving infrastructure, or data science workflows\n Experience with PostgreSQL and extensions such as pgvector for vector search applications\nExperience supporting DoD or IC programs, particularly AFRL, DARPA, or Space Force\n Familiarity with AWS GovCloud and FedRAMP compliance considerations\n \n\n \nWhy Work for Us?\n\n Core4ce is a team of innovators, self-starters, and critical thinkers—driven by a shared mission to strengthen national security and advance warfighting outcomes.\n\nWe offer:\n\n401(k) with 100% company match on the first 6% deferred, with immediate vesting\nComprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage—employee portion paid 100% by Core4ce\nUnlimited access to training and certifications, with no pre-set cap on eligible professional development\nTuition assistance for job-related degrees and courses\nPaid parental leave, PTO that grows with tenure, and generous holiday schedules\nGot a big idea? At Core4ce, The Forge gives every employee the chance to propose bold innovations and help bring them to life with internal backing.\n \n\nJoin us to build a career that matters—supported by a company that invests in you.\n\n \n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, disability, veteran status, age, genetic information, or other legally protected status.",
