      "Wellbeam Consumer Health logo\nSenior Shopify Developer (DTC / CRO-Focused) (Full Time Contractor)\nRemote, Remote, Remote, United States\nEmployees can work remotely\nFull-time\nCompensation: USD 60,000 - USD 80,000 - yearly\nCompany Description\nAt Wellbeam Consumer Health, we are inspired by our consumer. We are creating the leading ecommerce-focused consumer wellness business, delivering value-added products that help people thrive. We’re focused on dramatically accelerating existing brands as well as adding select, new digitally-native consumer wellness brands.\n\nThe current Wellbeam portfolio includes Eu Natural, a digitally-native provider of vitamin and mineral nutritional supplements; TruSkin, a leading skincare brand with a range of high quality, plant-powered products including the #1 best-selling facial serum on Amazon; and BioTRUST Nutrition, a fast-growing, leading eCommerce, nutrition brand with a portfolio of premium-quality, science-based products that focuses on making health living and health aging more accessible and enjoyable. Wellbeam is backed by American Pacific Group.\n\nJob Description\nRole: Senior Shopify Developer (DTC / CRO-Focused)\n\nObjective\n\nHire a senior, A-player Shopify developer to own our website experience end-to-end.\n\nPrimary goal:\n\nIncrease conversion rate and site performance\nShip high-quality landing pages quickly\nSupport full website rebuild + ongoing experimentation\nThis role replaces the need for an external agency and brings execution in-house.\n\nCore Responsibilities\n\n1. Landing Page Development (Primary Focus)\n\nBuild net-new landing pages from Figma\nTranslate designs into pixel-perfect, responsive Shopify pages\nImprove layouts, UX, and conversion during implementation\nCreate iterations / variants for testing\nExpectation:\n\nFast turnaround\nHigh quality\nCRO-minded execution (not just design replication)\n2. Shopify Development (Full Ownership)\n\nCustomize and extend Shopify theme (Liquid, JS, HTML/CSS)\nBuild reusable sections and templates\nImplement new functionality within Shopify architecture\nTroubleshoot bugs and fix issues quickly\n3. CRO & Experimentation\n\nImplement A/B tests and landing page variations\nIdentify opportunities to improve conversion\nOptimize funnels, PDPs, and landing experiences\n4. Site Performance & Technical Quality\n\nImprove site speed and Core Web Vitals\nEnsure clean, scalable, maintainable code\nOptimize mobile experience\n5. Website Rebuild Support\n\nContribute to full site refresh\nBuild new templates, structures, and components\nMaintain ongoing production while rebuild is in progress\nSuccess Criteria\n\nLanding pages are shipped quickly and consistently\nDeveloper can build a net-new page in hours, not days\nConversion rate improves over time\nSite speed and performance improve\nMinimal need for oversight or hand-holding\nActs as owner of the Shopify experience\nRequirements\n\nMust-Have\n\n5+ years Shopify development experience\nStrong in:\nShopify Liquid\nJavaScript\nHTML/CSS\nTheme architecture and customization\nExperience building DTC landing pages\nStrong understanding of:\nUX/UI\nCRO principles\nMobile-first design\nCapabilities Required\n\nCan take Figma designs → production-ready pages quickly\nCan improve layouts and flows independently\nBalances speed and quality\nStrong async communication (Slack, minimal meetings)\nNice-to-Have\n\nA/B testing tools (Convert, VWO, etc.)\nExperience with page builders (Replo, Shogun)\nSubscription platforms (Recharge, Skio)\nAnalytics setup (GA4, Meta Pixel)\nTechnical SEO knowledge\nExperience with $10M+ DTC brands\nWorking Model\n\nReports into: Founder / Growth team\nWorks closely with: Design (Figma-based workflow)\nCommunication: Slack, async-first\nMinimal meetings\nHigh ownership, fast execution environment\nCandidate Profile (What We Actually Want)\n\nSenior-level operator (not junior / mid)\nHas worked on high-performing DTC brands\nThinks in conversion, not just code\nFast executor with strong judgment\nCan operate independently without PM overhead\nWhat We Do NOT Want\n\nPure “ticket-taker” developers\nSlow, process-heavy agency-style devs\nPeople who only implement designs without thinking\nAnyone without real CRO / DTC experience\nCompensation & Structure\n\n$60K–$80K USD\nFull-time or contractor\nMust be North America-based\nHiring Notes\n\nPrioritize candidates with real DTC examples\nMust provide live Shopify sites or landing pages\nCRO thinking is a key filter (not optional)\nSpeed of execution is critical\n \n\n \n\nAdditional Information\nScreening Question (Required)\n\n“Walk me through a landing page you built that improved conversion rate. What did you change and why?”",
