      "Full Stack Engineer\nRemote with United States\nWe’re ALTEN Technology USA, an engineering company helping clients bring groundbreaking ideas to life—from advancing space exploration and life-saving medical devices to building autonomous electric vehicles. With 3,000+ experts across North America, we partner with leading companies in aerospace, medical devices, robotics, automotive, commercial vehicles, EVs, rail, and more.\n\nAs part of the global ALTEN Group—57,000+ engineers in 30 countries—we deliver across the entire product development cycle, from consulting to full project outsourcing.\n\nWhen you join ALTEN Technology USA, you’ll collaborate on some of the world’s toughest engineering challenges, supported by mentorship, career growth opportunities, and comprehensive benefits. We take pride in fostering a culture where employees feel valued, supported, and inspired to grow.\n\nLocation: Remote  within United States\n\nHours: Must be available during Pacific Standard Time (PST) business hours\n\n \n\nALTEN Technology is seeking a skilled Full Stack Developer to join the Web Engineering team supporting our client's digital presence across the US and EU markets. In this role, you will contribute to the development, optimization, and maintenance of their public-facing website, delivering high-performance, internationally localized web experiences. You will work closely with cross-functional stakeholders including design, marketing, and product teams to build scalable, content-driven web solutions.\n\n \n\nKey Responsibilities: \n\nDesign, develop, and maintain full stack web features for US and EU market websites\nBuild and integrate React-based front-end components with a focus on performance, accessibility, and responsiveness\nImplement and manage content delivery pipelines using Contentful CMS, including content modeling, API integrations, and localized content management for multiple regional markets\nDevelop and optimize server-side rendered (SSR) pages using Next.js to ensure fast load times, strong SEO performance, and scalable architecture\nCollaborate with UX/UI designers to translate wireframes and design specs into polished, production-ready web experiences\nSupport multi-region content strategies, including multi-language and multi-locale configurations within Contentful\nParticipate in code reviews, technical planning sessions, and agile ceremonies\nMonitor and improve Core Web Vitals, page performance, and cross-browser compatibility\nTroubleshoot, debug, and resolve production issues in a timely manner\nDocument technical implementations, component libraries, and integration workflows\n \n\nRequired Qualifications:\n\n5+ years of professional full stack web development experience\nStrong proficiency in React.js, including hooks, state management, and component architecture\nHands-on experience with Next.js, including SSR (Server-Side Rendering), SSG, and the App Router\nExperience working with Contentful CMS, including content modeling, REST/GraphQL API integration, and localization workflows\nProficiency in JavaScript (ES6+) and/or TypeScript\nSolid understanding of HTML5, CSS3, and responsive/mobile-first design principles\nExperience working with RESTful APIs and/or GraphQL\nFamiliarity with version control using Git and collaborative development workflows (e.g., GitHub/GitLab)\nStrong understanding of web performance best practices and SEO fundamentals\n \n\nPreferred Qualifications:\n\nExperience developing or maintaining automotive or consumer brand websites\nKnowledge of EU web regulations including GDPR compliance and accessibility standards (WCAG 2.1)\nExperience with CI/CD pipelines and deployment platforms such as Vercel or AWS\nFamiliarity with design systems and component libraries (e.g., Storybook, Tailwind CSS)\nWorking knowledge of Node.js for back-end API development or middleware\nExposure to analytics and A/B testing integrations (e.g., Google Tag Manager, Optimizely)\n \n\nSalary Range:  \n\n$95,000 - $110,000\nThe actual salary offered is dependent on various factors including, but not limited to, location, the candidate’s combination of job-related knowledge, qualifications, skills, education, training, and experience \nALTEN Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Our Policy is to extend opportunities to qualified applicants and employees on an equal basis regardless of an individual’s age, race, color, sex, religion, national origin, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression or veteran status.\n\nPlease beware of job seeker scams and see this important notice on our careers page for more information about our recruiting process.\n\nCompliance Notice: Alten USA is a federal contractor subject to the requirements of the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act (VEVRAA) and Executive Order 11246. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer and consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or veteran status.\n\nDrug Screening Requirement: As a federal contractor, Alten USA maintains a drug-free workplace. All candidates selected for employment will be required to successfully complete a pre-employment drug screening as a condition of hire.",
