    job_desc:
      "Software Engineering Intern - Identity\nRemote - US\nAbout the Identity Team:  \n\nThe Identity team owns the core services that power how members and workforce users securely access Transcarent experiences. This includes: \n\nMember Identity Services – login, registration, account recovery, and management of member identifiers across systems (user IDs, person IDs, membership IDs, etc.). \nWorkforce Identity Services – corporate identity and accounts for employees and partners using platforms like Okta and Ping \nSSO and Federation – inbound and outbound SSO for member apps and integrations with customers and partners. \nThe team builds and operates secure, highly available backend services and APIs running in modern cloud infrastructure, integrating with Okta, Ping Identity, and related tooling. \n\n____________________________________________________________________________________ \n\nWhat you’ll do:  \n\nWork on projects that impact the business and contribute directly to Transcarent’s mission of better health and care by making it easy and safe for members and employees to sign in and access our products. \nHelp design, build, and test features in our Identity and Access Management services, including login, registration, account recovery, and SSO/federation workflows for member and workforce users. \nContribute to backend services that integrate with Ping and AWS/GCP infrastructure, focusing on reliability, performance, and security. \nSupport projects around environment and tooling for our identity platform (e.g., improving non-prod and sandbox environments, automation, and observability) to enable safe, repeatable changes.  \nParticipate in the full engineering lifecycle: design discussions, code reviews, writing tests, monitoring services, and responding to issues as part of an on-call/support culture. \nCollaborate with engineers across web, mobile, platform, data, and security teams to deliver secure and delightful sign-in experiences. \nYou’ll gain exposure to how a real engineering team works, from sprint planning to shipping code, and you’ll have a formal mentor on the Identity team guiding you throughout your internship period. \n\nWhat we’re looking for: \n\nCurrently pursuing a degree in Computer Science or a related field. \nProficiency in at least one modern programming language such as Go, Java, Python, or TypeScript \nInterest in security, compliance, and privacy and how those shape real-world identity platforms. \nExcellent verbal and written communication skills. \nStrong problem-solving skills & attention to detail \nWillingness to learn and adapt in a fast-paced environment \nNice to have \n\nFamiliarity with cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, Azure) \nExposure to identity platforms such as Okta, Ping Identity / PingOne, Auth0, or AWS IAM / IAM Identity Center \nUnderstanding of CI/CD pipelines, and Git-based workflows. \nAbout Our Internship Program\nWe're excited to offer a hands-on internship experience designed to give you real-world exposure and meaningful work from day one. Our summer program runs May 26 – August 14, giving you a structured, full-season experience alongside talented teams across the business. We're looking for curious, driven individuals who are eager to learn, contribute, and grow. If that sounds like you, we'd love to hear from you!\n \nProgram Details:\n:date: Duration: May 26 – August 14\n:moneybag: Compensation: Competitive hourly rate (role dependent) we do not provide relocation assistance\n:no_entry_sign: Benefits: Internship roles are not eligible for Full-Time employee benefits\n:earth_americas: Work Authorization: Candidates must be independently authorized to work in the U.S. — we are unable to provide sponsorship or work authorization for this position\n \n\nWho we are  \n\nTranscarent is the One Place for Health and Careᵀᴹ, bringing medical, pharmacy, and point solutions together with the WayFindingᵀᴹ experience, the first and only generative AI-powered health and care platform for health consumers. Our WayFinding experience, paired with transparent and consumer-driven pharmacy care, 2nd.MD expert medical opinions, and virtual primary care, works seamlessly with comprehensive Care Experiences – Cancer Care, Surgery Care, and Weight Health – to support people with all of their health needs, simple or serious. More than 1,700 employers and health plans rely on us to provide information, guidance, and care, empowering health consumers with more choice, an experience they love, access to higher-quality care, and lower costs for 21 million Members. For more information, visit transcarent.com, and follow us on LinkedIn. \n\nAt Transcarent, our values guide everything we do:\n\nPeople First: We prioritize our Members, clients, and each other in every decision\nCare: Every decision starts with improving health and care for our Members\nResilience: We push boundaries and take the uncharted path to change an industry\nResults: We take ownership, solve with speed, and deliver for our people and each other\nHumble and Human: We lead with humility, bring fun to tough moments, and go further together\nTotal Rewards \n\nIndividual compensation packages are based on a few different factors unique to each candidate, including primary work location and an evaluation of a candidate’s skills, experience, market demands, and internal equity.  \n\nSalary is just one component of Transcarent's total package. All regular employees are also eligible for the corporate bonus program or a sales incentive (target included in OTE) as well as stock options.  \n\nOur benefits and perks programs include, but are not limited to:  \n\nCompetitive medical, dental, and vision coverage  \nCompetitive 401(k) Plan with a generous company match  \nFlexible Time Off/Paid Time Off, 13 paid holidays  \nProtection Plans including Life Insurance, Disability Insurance, and Supplemental Insurance \nMental Health and Wellness benefits  \nTranscarent is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. If you are a person with a disability and require assistance during the application process, please don’t hesitate to reach out!  \n\nResearch shows that candidates from underrepresented backgrounds often don’t apply unless they meet 100% of the job criteria. While we have worked to consolidate the minimum qualifications for each role, we aren’t looking for someone who checks each box on a page; we’re looking for active learners and people who care about disrupting the current health and care with their unique experiences. ",
