      "Full-Stack Engineer\nRemote · Full time\nCompany website\nApply for Full-Stack Engineer\nJoin our team as a Full-Stack Engineer, and play a key role in building the first-ever AI-powered sales development platform that blends automation and human intelligence!\n\nAbout Vox Labs\nScale your pipeline. Without scaling your team. AI + Human symbiosis, for selling.\nDescription\n💫 Full-Stack Engineer 💫\n📍 Location: Remote\n\nVox Labs Website | LinkedIn\n\n\n\n🏗️ Why work with us\nVox Labs (by Spyglass Software, Inc.) is building the next-generation AI-powered sales development platform, designed to blend automation and human intelligence to drive pipeline at scale.\n\n\n\nWe’re looking for an entrepreneurial engineer with 4+ years of software engineering experience to help us build the foundation of a venture-backed startup.\n\n\n\nThis is a unique opportunity to be a core member of a company redefining how teams prospect, working side-by-side with our founding team to shape both the product and the future of AI-driven sales development.\n\n\n\nWe've raised $2.5M in pre-seed from Notation Capital, 8-Bit Capital, CoFound Partners and V1.VC with deep team expertise in enterprise software and sales.\n\n\n\n🧑‍💻 What You’ll Work On\nAs a Full-Stack Engineer at Vox Labs, you’ll work directly with our CEO, founding team and early customers to build a next generation platform that transforms sales prospecting into an intelligent, automated process.\n\n\n\n🚀 Your impact:\n\nBuild and scale our AI-powered sales platform, from backend data processing to the frontend user experience.\nWork across our entire platform, including our React-based frontend, Node.js backend, CI/CD infrastructure, VOIP APIs and machine learning components.\nDefine the architecture, tech stack, and feature roadmap alongside our leadership team.\nExperiment with LLMs, automation workflows, and real-time analytics to enhance sales prospecting efficiency.\nBe at the forefront of AI-human collaboration, shaping the next wave of intelligent sales tooling.\n\n\n✅ Requirements\nStrong knowledge of software development principles and ability to execute independently in a fast-moving environment.\nExperience and preference for working across the full stack (backend, frontend, databases, and cloud services).\nDemonstrated ability to learn new technologies quickly and contribute across different parts of the stack.\nInterest in real-time APIs, large-scale machine learning, and CPaaS systems (like Twilio).\nOk with shipping fast, making mistakes and learning even faster. Rapid iterations over delayed perfection.\n\n\n🔭 What we look for\nHigh-potential, raw talent.\nCuriosity, mischief, and intensity.\nHistory of building useful things.\n\n\n💸 Compensation\n\nOur compensation packages are based on a wide array of factors including your unique skill set, years of experience, and preferred total compensation ratio between salary and equity.\n\n\n\nDay-to-day remote works for us, but we think it's important to get to know your colleagues outside of the typical Slack and Google Meet chats. In the past, this means meeting up in person in San Francisco and New York and spending a week together.\n\n\n\nWe offer healthcare and 401k with matching.\n\n\n\n$140k - $160k salary range + significant equity.\n\n\n\n🚴 Interview process\n30 minute call with Co-founder & CEO to discuss background, experience, career goals, and answer questions\n2-3 hour technical assessment (build an app with the Star Wars API, or another similar project)\n30 minutes with a member of our engineering team\n2-3 hour technical interview (and potentially coming to you to meet in person)\nReference checks\nOffer extended\n\n\n🕵️ Who You’ll Work With\n\n\nI'm Nick, founder and CEO of Spyglass Software, Inc. I've spent the last decade scaling high-performing sales teams and optimizing sales processes at fast-growing startups. I'm passionate about leveraging AI and automation to transform sales development, making prospecting more intelligent and scalable. Outside of work, I enjoy road biking and obsessing over my daily macronutrient ratios.\n\n\n\nI'm Dar, founding engineer. Based in Atlanta, I've built scalable systems at both startups and large enterprises, working across the full stack to develop everything from high-performance backend services to intuitive frontend applications. When I'm not coding, you can find me gaming, leading D&D campaigns, or exploring the latest advancements in tech.\n\n\n\nI'm Michael, founding engineer. Based in Brooklyn, I've been a hacker my whole life—breaking, building, and experimenting with technology to push its limits. I've worked across the full stack, from low-level systems to scalable cloud applications, always looking for new ways to optimize and automate. When I'm not deep in code, you can find me hanging out with my cat(s), exploring security exploits, or breaking things just to figure out how to put them back together.\n\n\n\nSalary\n$120,000 - $160,000 per year",
