      "Welcome to the Block!\nSr. React Native Engineer\nRemote · Part time\nApply for Sr. React Native Engineer\nAs a member of this team, you will be responsible for rebuilding our application using React Native and React Native Web.\n\nAbout Welcome to the Block!\nTradeblock's mission is to increase access to collectibles by making acquisition more affordable, and to make the practice of collecting more active, engaging, and communal. In doing so, we aim to inspire, support and develop the next generation of entrepreneurs with a heavy focus on diversity and an equitable workplace for all team members.\nDescription\nTradeBlock is expanding rapidly and we are looking for a highly skilled engineer to join our React Native development team. As a member of this team, you will be responsible for rebuilding our application using React Native and React Native Web. The ideal candidate should have a solid background in building applications with React Native, with working experience in, Expo, Solito, Next.JS, Native Base, Reanimated/Moti and GraphQL. Ideally, you will also have experience working with Swift on iOS and Java on Android. \n\n\n\nRequirements:\n\n \n\n4+ years of experience developing JavasScript based software\n3+ years of experience working with React and React native\nWorking knowledge of Next.JS react framework\nExtensive knowledge of Node.JS\nWork experience RESTful APIs, GraphQL\nExperienced with building and using reusable components \nExperience or desire working in a small team, fast-paced startup atmosphere\nWorking experience with Expo\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n \n\nFocus on developing and maintaining our new mono repo React Native app for iOS, Android, and Web.\nAssist in debugging production issues across the application stack\nMaintain, modify and extend the existing Native Base component library with custom styling implementation\nWork on implementing animations, and gestures logic\nCollaborate with product managers during daily standup, grooming, and clarification sessions as part of an agile process\nCollaborate with other engineers on day to day work and activities\nShare and apply knowledge between other team members\nHelp improve standards, tooling, and processes\n \n\n\n\n \n\nNice to haves:\n\n \n\nBachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or similar\nFamiliar with various approaches to stress testing for scale\nExperience with Algolia AI search engine \nExperience with CI/CD automation for mobile apps and web\nPassion for sneakers, aka a sneakerhead\n\n\nBenefits:\n\n\n\nFully remote work with occasional office visits in Austin, TX\n\n\nAbout Tradeblock\n\n \n\nTradeblock is the leading Sneaker Trading Platform and Community that enables collectors to use sneakers as currency by becoming a part of a virtual community. Our main focus is to deliver an advanced digital trading experience and to foster and nurture collector communities nationwide.\n\n \n\nHeadquartered in Austin, TX, Tradeblock launched their cross-platform mobile app in May 2021, and by the end of the year, it had grown to over 100,000 members. In June 2021, Tradeblock was honored as part of Forbes Next 1000 Class of 2021, and by November, we successfully closed our seed funding round, led by Trinity Ventures. Additionally, Tradeblock received a grant from the Google for Startups Black Founders Fund. As a startup founded by a minority, diversity and inclusion are central to our mission.\n\n \n\nWe believe our hustle, hunger, and integrity is what will set Tradeblock apart and are looking for like-minded individuals to join the team!\n\n\n\n\n\nTradeblock is an equal opportunity employer.\n\n",
