      "Vijil, Inc\nSoftware Development Engineer, Trustworthy AI\nRemote · Full time\nApply for Software Development Engineer, Trustworthy AI\nVijil is looking for a Senior Software Engineer to develop methods for improving the security and safety of large language models.\n\nAbout Vijil, Inc\nVijil is an AI software startup on a mission to help organizations build and operate autonomous agents that they can trust. Founded by technologists who built the deep learning platform in Amazon SageMaker at AWS and established responsible AI practices at Twitch and Splunk, Vijil is helping AI developers build-in trust into open-source large language models. If you're passionate about improving the explainability, security, and safety of neural networks that will be used in business-critical applications over the next decade, you'll enjoy making an impact at Vijil. Join us today to grow with the company and its products and customers.\nDescription\nAbout Us\n\nVijil is a venture-funded AI software startup on a mission to help organizations build and operate intelligent agents that people can trust. We are building tools and services to enable AI developers to continuously improve the security and safety of custom large language models.\n\n\n\nAbout the Role\n\nAs a software developer at Vijil, you will build upon the latest research methods in trustworthy ML and generative AI to deliver cloud services to AI developers who are customizing LLMs with enterprise-specific data. You will collaborate with applied scientists and technologists to build capabilities for testing, tuning, and deploying LLMs with security and safety. Your day-to-day responsibilities include:\n\nWorking closely with applied scientists, academic collaborators, and senior leaders, and prospective users to solve problems facing enterprises that want to deploy LLMs in production\nImplementing methods to detect LLM vulnerabilities to attacks such as prompt injection, PII disclosure, model evasion, jailbreaking, and model extraction.\nImplementing methods to assess LLM propensities for harm such as toxicity, unfair, and unethical behavior\nDesigning and developing new techniques to reduce vulnerabilities to attack and mitigate propensities for harms\n\n\nAbout You\n\nYou take ownership of your customer's problem, dive deep into root causes, invent new methods anchored in CS/AI/ML first principles to address the problem, deliver rapid results, and continuously enhance the customer's experience. As part of a highly collaborative team, you rely on your exceptional (written and verbal) communication skills to inform and persuade. You have a strong analytical mind, you approach challenges with a problem-solving stance, and you have the grit and resilience to deal with setbacks. You find this work meaningful because you know deeply that we need to build trust into AI/ML systems from the inside-out in order to realize their transformative potential. \n\n\n\nMinimum Qualifications\n\nMS or Ph D in Computer Science, Applied Math, or equivalent discipline\n8+ years industry experience as an SDE or equivalent job\n2+ years experience in systems for LLM training and tuning.\n4+ years experience with training or inference of NLP models.\n4+ years experience with ML frameworks: TensorFlow, PyTorch, JAX.\nDemonstrable proficiency in programming with Python, Java, or C++ (GitHub link appreciated)\nProven competence in software engineering practices (version control, unit testing, documentation, code review, deployment, operations, on-call rotation, customer engagement)\nProven ability to work collaboratively with research scientists\nDemonstrable written and verbal communication skills (writing samples appreciated)\n\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\nMS or Ph D in Machine Learning, NLU, Neural Networks, or equivalent\nExperience with building LLMs or agents.\nFamiliarity with adversarial ML, LLM red-teaming, or responsible AI\nExperience working with cloud services on AWS, Azure, or GCP\n\n\nBenefits\n\nCompetitive base pay and equity.\nHealth, dental, and vision insurance plans.\nFlexible time-off policy.\nPaid parental and family leave.\nImmigration sponsorship.\n\n\nHow to Apply\n\nIf you are excited about making a meaningful impact on mechanisms to improve the security of generative AI models, please submit your resume and any examples of your relevant work. For any questions, email us at hiring@vijil.ai.\n\n\n\nVijil is an equal opportunity employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws pertaining to fair employment practices.\n\n\n\nSalary\n$150,000 - $200,000 per year",
    company: "Vijil, Inc",
    title: "Software Development Engineer, Trustworthy AI",
    remote: "true",
    createdAt: "2026-04-04 02:37:03.765",
    createdById: "5",
