      "The Styled by Collective\nSenior Full Stack Engineer – Remote, US-Based\nRemote · Full time\nCompany website\nApply for Senior Full Stack Engineer – Remote, US-Based\nFirst engineering hire responsible for architecting, building, and scaling a full-stack ERP and digital wardrobe platform that powers luxury retail, consignment, and styling experiences.\n\nAbout The Styled by Collective\nThe Styled by Collective is a bespoke luxury personal styling company that caters to discerning clients seeking personalized and exclusive styling services. Our innovative blend of digital and onsite styling assures that every client receives tailored fashion solutions that enhance their personal style. By forging strong relationships with major retailers, we provide our clients with access to unique consignment shopping options and a curated palette of sartorial choices. Our deep commitment to quality, trend awareness, and exceptional client service sets us apart in the competitive styling market.\nDescription\nThe Styled by Collective is a fashion-tech company on the frontier of transforming personalized styling and inventory management in the luxury retail space. Blending elite human expertise with advanced technology, we’re building a new infrastructure for how people shop, style, and manage their wardrobes.\n\n\n\nAs we evolve from private client services to SaaS, our proprietary platform—Sartoria—is redefining consignment and ERP operations by enabling secure, scalable, and data-driven styling at scale. Sartoria isn’t just a digital wardrobe; it’s the trust infrastructure powering high-touch, high-value experiences across retail, logistics, and luxury service.\n\n\n\nWhat We’re Building\n\n\n\nOur ERP and inventory system solves problems traditional platforms ignore:\n\n\n\nBlind Inventory & Consignment Ordering: Tracks high-value transactions (often $100K–$300K+) in environments without upfront payment or POS-based records, offering retailers, stylists, and clients a secure, verifiable pipeline.\nRetailer & Personal Shopping Integration: Consolidates purchases across Net-a-Porter, Saks, Moda Operandi, etc., allowing AI-assisted recommendations and in-store experiences where client wishlists become real-time pre-selections.\nPayment & Compliance Innovation: Solves compliance and manual credit workflows with a fintech-integrated architecture designed for blind inventory commerce—improving both speed and security.\n\n\nWe’re at a pivotal moment: building a category-defining product that solves backend inefficiencies while delivering world-class UX to our discerning client base. You’ll work directly with our CTO as the first engineering hire, owning platform architecture, implementation, and scale from day one.\n\n\n\nOur Stack: Full-stack TypeScript (via React and Bun/Node.js), PostgreSQL, Redis, Docker, AWS, Temporal\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote. Full-time, US-based applicants only (within contiguous US timezones)\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\n\n\nHelp lead the design and implementation of our next-gen digital wardrobe and ERP system\nDevelop performant front-ends and scalable, secure back-ends—powering everything from styling algorithms to fintech integrations.\nTackle hard problems in consignment logic, high-value transaction handling, and real-time inventory reconciliation.\nEstablish engineering best practices, performance standards, and an ethos rooted in craft, ownership, education, and velocity.\n\n\nYou’re a Great Fit If You\n\n\n\nThrive in a fast-paced, zero-bureaucracy environment that rewards initiative, ownership, and hard work\nWant the rare opportunity to help build an ambitious greenfield product with massive market potential\nAre excited about creating full stack systems that actually make businesses run\n\n\nRequirements\n\n\n\nBachelor’s Degree in Computer Science or Engineering\n5+ years of full-stack engineering experience\n3+ years shipping consumer-facing products\nProficiency in TypeScript or JavaScript, and at least one other statically typed language\nProficiency with a SQL database (does not need to be PostgreSQL)\nStrong communication skills and the ability to explain technical concepts clearly to non-technical stakeholders\nA passion for product, an eye for detail, and a bias for action\nA good understanding of how to use LLMs responsibly and the perils of blindly consuming their output\n\n\nBonus Points\n\n\n\nExperience with AWS, GCP, or Azure\nExperience with macOS (we are not currently maintaining local environments on other OSes, sorry!)\nPrior startup experience\nInterest in fashion or styling (not required—our team has that covered, and yes, we have merch 😎)\n\n\nWhy Join Us\n\n\n\nCompetitive Comp Package: Salary + meaningful equity\nFull Benefits: Health insurance, 401k, unlimited PTO\nImpact & Ownership: First engineering hire with full-stack autonomy and product influence\nProven Growth: 7-figure ARR business with high-net-worth clients and strong market demand\nFuture-Shaping Work: Be part of building the tech platform that redefines luxury retail from the inside out",
