      "Python/Transact SQL Software Engineer\nPhoenix, AZ, US\nYesterday\nRequisition ID: 1010\n\nApply\nSUMMARY\n\nIntellimed is a Healthcare company providing access to a broad spectrum of healthcare claim and discharge encounter data. This data includes office visits, outpatient surgeries, and hospital inpatient data at a detailed claim level. We process over 800 million claims quarterly. The applications we provide are web-based and include our own developed ad-hoc data mart, dashboard visualizations, Tableau workbooks, and more. Our customers include Hospital Systems, Medical device manufacturers, Physician groups, insurers, etc.\n\nThis role will be instrumental in the continuous development and improvement of our internal data processing and customer-facing applications, and will have creative control over methodology, business logic layer, Agentic AI development for automating data processing, and will be involved in the entire end-to-end process of the SAAS hosted applications.\n\nWhat we are looking for:\n\n Expertise with Python and Pycharm. (Required)\n Expertise with GitHub for source control. (Required)\n Extensive experience with ANSI SQL stored procedures in MariaDB, MySQL, or Oracle (Required)\n Must have permanent residency status in the USA.\n Experience with Java Script (Is a plus)\n Experience with REACT. (Is a plus)\n Experience with Healthcare data. (Is a plus)\n Minimum 2 years experience as Python and Transact SQL programming (Required)\nKey responsibilities include:\n\nDeveloping, testing, and maintaining applications using Python.\nDesigning, optimizing, and maintaining complex T-SQL queries, stored procedures, and functions.\nCollaborating with cross-functional teams (e.g., data scientists, analysts, front-end developers) to define requirements and deliver solutions.\nPerforming data extraction, transformation, and loading (ETL) processes.\nTroubleshooting application and database performance issues and ensuring data integrity and security.\nDeveloping scripts for task automation and system integration.\nCreating and maintaining technical documentation and specifications.\nRequired Skills & Qualifications\n\nA strong candidate for a Python and T-SQL role will possess a blend of programming and database expertise:\n\nProficiency in Python: Strong command of Python programming for backend development, data processing, and automation.\nStrong SQL/T-SQL Expertise: Experience with writing and optimizing complex queries, joins, CTEs, views, and stored procedures.\nDatabase Knowledge: In-depth knowledge of relational databases (e.g., Microsoft SQL Server) and data modeling principles.\nProblem-Solving Abilities: Strong analytical and problem-solving skills to diagnose and resolve software and data issues.\nRelevant Tools: ETL Tools (Navicat), Git, PyCharm or similar IDE. AI tools Claude, etc.\nWhat we offer:\n\n Full-time remote work with flexible work schedules. \n Competitive starting salary commensurate with experience.\n Potential bonus pay based on company performance.\n Healthcare is a vast, fast-growing industry. We work with data for all aspects of the medical life cycle\n Comprehensive Benefits Package which includes:\nQuality health insurance plans\nTraditional 401K plan + match\nVision, dental, disability, and life insurance\nFlexible Spending Accounts and Health Savings Accounts\nGenerous PTO\n",
