      "Full Stack Engineer - Client facing (Laravel / React) - (GMT-6/-5/-4)\nRemote\n \n\nAt Workwize, we’re revolutionizing how businesses support their global teams. \n\nAt Workwize, we’re helping IT teams to easily equip their remote and global teams with all necessary IT equipment. Our automated SaaS platform simplifies hardware deployment, management, and retrieval with fast, reliable deliveries in 100+ countries.\n\nWith 50.000 users and 120.000 devices under management, we’re solving hybrid work challenges like laptop deliveries, returns and equipment tracking, allowing IT teams to focus less on manual hassles and more on strategic initiatives.\n\nJoin our team to help shape the future of global collaboration. At Workwize, your work will make a real impact in building smarter, more connected workplaces worldwide.\n\nLinkedIn has also recognised Workwize as one of the Top 10 Startups for 2025 in the Netherlands!\n\n \n\nLinkedIn Top Startups 2025 - Logo Transparent\n\nDo you want to make a positive impact and directly contribute to the improvement of remote working for companies around the world? Are you a person which like to build software product for cool clients such as Otrium, Mollie and Catawiki? Continue reading to see if the Sr. Full-Stack Developer role at Workwize is something for you!\n\n \n\nYour role\n\nWe are always looking for Laravel focused full-stack engineers to join our product team in Amsterdam. We’re a company in hyper growth fase, with a robust product that thousands of people use to setup their remote workspaces.\n\nWe are looking for someone who will able to join our team of both remote and hybrid engineers working on both front-end and back-end positions in making the right architectural decision, and bringing our platform to the next level.\n\nTogether with your team you will work on building best-in-class product experiences for customers. You will be working together with the team create and design your own re-usable APIs and components.\n\nOur core platform is built on Laravel (backend) and React.js (frontend). We are constantly coming up with new features to continue building our platform and expand our product offering.\n\nOur Team\n\nBecoming part of Workwize means making an impact. We make sure that we will contribute to the change in the way of working. For us it is also important that we make an impact on our employees, that they feel challenged and ease. We consist of a rapid growing and ambitious team with all different backgrounds. Entrepreneurs, Operational specialists, Developers, Sales gurus you can find them all at Workwize and are always on the look-out for the next original ideas to reach more consumers and create the best value for our customers.\n\nWe are looking forward to meeting you and see if there is a match with the Workwize team!\n\nExperience / Skills\n\nAt least a Bachelor with background in tech or equivalent based on work experience\n8 years work experience with the Laravel and React frameworks\nExperience building applications with Javascript/Typescript, PHP, HTML5, CSS and MySQL 8\nPassionate about usability, user experience, beauty and elegance of UI's\nEager to learn, discuss and share knowledge with the rest of the teams\nNice to have: knowledge of Kubernetes, Docker, and other tools user in DevOps\nAbsolute fan of TDD and CI/CD pipelines\nStrong track record of leading technical projects and coordinating teams of 3+ engineers\nExperience mentoring and supporting the professional growth of fellow engineers\nBackground in product-based companies with multiple product and engineering teams\nProven track record of driving engineering initiatives that impacted other teams or the wider organization\nExcellent presentation and communication skills, with the ability to clearly explain technical concepts and join customer calls when needed\nSkills\n\nYou’re an engineer, always interested in new technologies, pushing your boundaries and challenging others.\nYou're fluent in business English, both written and verbal\nCritical thinking and initiative: Hands-on, nothing-is-impossible mindset\nEnjoy working with teams with multidisciplinary backgrounds\nExperience working in dynamic environments, such as a startup or scaleup environment\nStrong user-orientation and communication skills\nPro-active attitude, go-get mentality\nAnalytical, troubleshooting skills\nStructured, able to clearly define, prioritize and plan your own tasks\nCommitment to deliver quality (first time right) and on-time\nMotivated and enthusiastic team player, supporting your colleagues\nKeen to learn and further develop your expertise\n \n\n \n\nWorkwize Offers: \n\n• Flexible hybrid work environment.\n• Top-notch tools and equipment provided.\n• Vibrant, entrepreneurial culture with opportunities for growth.\n• Off-sites and multi-yearly team bonding events.\n• Team lunches and surprise events to keep things fun.\n• Pension scheme.\n• Classpass corporate membership.",
