      "Senior Software Engineer\nRemote\nFull Time\nExperienced\nYOUR MISSION: Your mission is to build and evolve the Dispatch platform that connects our customers with the right service providers during roadside incidents. Dispatch is at the heart of how Urgently delivers real-time assistance, and this role owns the feasibility, design, and delivery of Dispatch capabilities with a strong focus on reliability, speed, and operational quality.  You’ll work closely with Product and Operations to ensure Dispatch decisions are accurate, scalable, and resilient under real-world conditions. \n\nYOUR LEGACY: Your legacy will be the stability, scalability, and evolution of the Dispatch platform. This includes building and maintaining core Dispatch services, improving provider assignment and workflows, and raising the bar on system reliability and operational excellence for one of Urgently’s most mission-critical systems. The result?  You helped Urgently become the world’s leading mobility assistance company.   \n\nWHAT YOU’LL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR:   \n\n1) First 2 months: \n\nRamp up on Urgently’s platform architecture, development environment, and engineering philosophy \nDevelop a strong understanding of the Dispatch system, including provider assignment, workflows, integrations, and operational dependencies \nBecome productive in the Dispatch codebase, deployment process, and on-call/operational workflows \n2) First 6 months: \n\nFully understand the mission and business goals of the Dispatch platform \nTake ownership of the development and stability of core Dispatch services \nPartner closely with Product to design and deliver Dispatch features, working through requirements, tradeoffs, and edge cases \nImprove Dispatch services using modern, scalable approaches while maintaining performance and reliability \n3) Ongoing...  \n\nDesign, build, and evolve features within the Dispatch system \nOwn Dispatch services end to end: development, deployment, monitoring, and operational stability \nParticipate in day-to-day execution while influencing longer-term technical direction for Dispatch \nWHO YOU ARE: \n\nTechnical Foundation  \n\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a related technical field \n7+ years of software development experience in backend, distributed systems environments \nStrong, hands-on experience with: \nJava and the Java ecosystem \nSpring Boot, Spring MVC, and microservices architecture \nData structures and core algorithms \nMySQL and NoSQL data stores \nUnit and system testing frameworks \nGit and modern version control workflows \nProblem Solving & Creativity \n\nCreative thinker and strong problem solver who can navigate ambiguity \nAble to work through complex Dispatch scenarios and propose clear, practical solutions \nPartners with Product to shape solutions, not just implement tickets \nProactively identifies issues and improvement opportunities before they impact operations \nOwnership & Accountability \n\nStrong ownership mindset for mission-critical Dispatch systems \nTakes responsibility for quality, performance, and real-world system behavior \nComfortable operating and supporting the services they build, including incident follow-ups \nTechnical Leadership \n\nActs as a technical leader within the Dispatch domain \nMentors' engineers and raises the bar for design, code quality, and system reliability \nClearly articulates designs, tradeoffs, and implementation plans to the broader team \nExecution \n\nDetail-oriented with a strong emphasis on maintainability and documentation \nBalances delivery speed with correctness, resilience, and scalability \nMakes pragmatic decisions aligned with both technical and business needs \nNice to Have Experience: \n\nExperience with Apache Solr / Elasticsearch \nExperience with Test-Driven Development \nExperience with logistics software (delivery, transportation, route planning) \nTHE NITTY GRITTY: \n\nLocation = Great news!  This position is remote and you have the option of working from anywhere in the U.S.!  \nManager = You’ll report to Senior Technical Lead \nCompensation =  The base salary range for this  position is $130,000 - $160,000. The range displayed on each job posting reflects the minimum and maximum target for new hire salaries for the position across all US locations. Within the range, individual pay is determined by job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. \nBenefits = At Urgently, we have awesome benefits!  We provide short term disability, long term disability, and life insurance to you - all free of charge! We also offer three different medical plans to choose from, two dental plans , a vision plan, and other valuable benefits. You’ll have 12 holidays off and unlimited paid time off.  We match 100% on the first 3% you contribute to our 401(k)and then 50% of the next 2% you contribute. So, if you contribute 5% of your paycheck, we’ll match 4% of that.  Free money! \nOUR FAIR HIRING PRACTICES:\n\nAt Urgently, we don’t just accept difference - we celebrate it, we support it, and we thrive on it for the benefit of our employees, our customers and the communities where we operate. We are an equal opportunity employer which means that employment and advancement at Urgently is based on a person's merit and qualifications.\n\n\nWe do not discriminate against any applicant or employee on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, religion, creed, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, breastfeeding or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender, gender identity or expression, physical or mental disability, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local law.\n\n\nYou should also know that we adhere to these same principles in all aspects of employment, including, but not limited to, recruitment, hiring, job assignment, compensation, promotion, access to benefits and training, discipline, and termination of employment.\n\n\nApplicants with disabilities may be entitled to reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act and similar applicable state laws. Please let us know if you need assistance completing any forms or to otherwise participate in the application process\n\n\nFor more information visit www.geturgently.com",
