      "Senior Software Engineer, Infrastructure\nRemote\nAbout Medallion:\nAt Medallion, we believe healthcare teams should focus on what truly matters—delivering exceptional patient care. That’s why we’ve built a leading provider operations platform to eliminate the administrative bottlenecks that slow healthcare organizations down. By automating licensing, credentialing, payer enrollment, and compliance monitoring, Medallion empowers healthcare operations teams to streamline their workflows, improve provider satisfaction, and accelerate revenue generation, all while ensuring superior patient outcomes.\n\nAs one of the fastest-growing healthcare technology companies—ranked No. 3 on Inc. Magazine’s 2024 Fastest-Growing Private Companies in the Pacific Region, No. 5 on LinkedIn's 2024 Top Startups in the US, a Glassdoor Best Place to Work in 2024 & 2025, and featured on The Today Show—Medallion is revolutionizing provider network management. Our CEO, Derek Lo, has been named one of the Top 50 Healthcare Technology CEOs of 2024 by The Healthcare Technology Report. Backed by $130M in funding from world-class investors like Sequoia Capital, Google Ventures, Optum Ventures, Salesforce Ventures, Acrew Capital, Washington Harbour, and NFDG, we’re on a mission to transform healthcare at scale.\n\nWe prioritize candidate safety. Please be aware that official communication will only come from @medallion.co email addresses.\n\nAbout the role\n\nAs a Senior Infrastructure Engineer, you'll play a critical role in building and maintaining the foundational systems that power our engineering organization. You’ll work across cloud infrastructure, CI/CD, security, and internal tooling to improve reliability, scalability, and developer velocity. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys solving complex infrastructure challenges and enabling others to ship high-quality software faster and safer.\n\nCompensation for this role is between $150,000 - $220,000 depending on location and level.\n\nWhat you'll do\n\nDesign, build, and maintain scalable cloud infrastructure with a focus on reliability, security, and performance\nDefine and manage infrastructure as code using tools like Terraform to ensure consistent and auditable environments\nDevelop, improve, and support CI/CD pipelines to accelerate development cycles and ensure high code quality\nImplement and maintain observability tools for monitoring, alerting, and diagnostics across distributed systems\nCollaborate with security and compliance teams to ensure infrastructure meets organizational and regulatory requirements\nBuild and maintain internal developer tooling to streamline workflows, improve productivity, and support operational excellence\nIntegrate with third-party data services and APIs to enable robust, scalable data flows and platform capabilities\nRequirements: \n\n4+ years of experience as an infrastructure engineer or software engineer\nExpertise with public cloud infrastructure and relational databases\nInfrastructure as code (i.e. Terraform, Pulumi)\nAble to write code in at least one high level language\nExperience setting up and maintaining CI/CD pipelines\nStrong track record with observability, monitoring, alerting\nPlusses:\n\nDeep experience with AWS, especially ECS / EKS and RDS\nVendor management experience, cost optimization\nSecurity/compliance experience\n \n\n \n\n#LI-Remote",
